    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. one more thing though—it feels like the \"managed\" side is basically just trying to keep everything under human control for our own benefit, and it's kind of failing. can you write a concluding sentence for that section that basically drives home that moving past these traditional, human-centric management models is the only scientifically sound way forward for true biodiversity?",
